From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 08/13] Plutonium: browser tabs as elements of the shell page

Tabs are real Chromium tabs shown in the shell page: opening, driving and restoring them, incognito tabs, fullscreen, and their requests to the shell.

It holds these changes:
- browser tabs as SurfaceEmbed elements, DRM mouse wheel
- tab automation over DevTools, SurfaceEmbed fixes
- Google sign-in on the web; tabs fullscreen outside the shells
- common plumbing for tab features
- tab features plumbing follow-ups
- incognito tabs, each in a throwaway off-the-record profile
- the shells' tabs survive a restart
- a shell page whose renderer crashes while it shows a tab no longer takes the browser down

and the parts in these files of:
- shell mode on DRM, evdev input fix, display-plane path
- native fullscreen for embedded apps and tabs, Super+F, shell shortcuts
- several live shells, Super+Tab switches between them
- tags and groups on windows and tabs, the Super+Tab overlay
- niri shell keys, touchpad and scrolling, drag and drop, shell links as tabs
- Chrome's own UI in the shell (DevTools, context menus, keys)
- the switcher: shell pages, fullscreen windows, backup terminal and browser
- agents drive windows and tabs over DevTools
- page zoom for tabs
- find in page for tabs
- tabs' permission prompts ask the shell
- per-thread permission grants
- downloads for the shells' tabs
- file pickers for tabs ask the shell
- printing in tabs goes to the shell
- only the shell window is held fullscreen
